{"_id":"68a736358ec3d8323af1dc08","nodeId":"fq2NMV-QV9ayJl82ZWzov","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# Queue\n\nQueue follows FIFO (First-In-First-Out) ordering where elements are added at one end and removed from the other. Rust doesn't have a built-in queue, but `VecDeque` provides queue functionality with `push_back()` for adding and `pop_front()` for removing elements efficiently.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"VecDeque in std::collections","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/collections/struct.VecDeque.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd08"},{"type":"official","title":"Queues","url":"https://docs.rs/queues/latest/queues/","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd09"},{"type":"article","title":"Working with Queues in Rust","url":"https://basillica.medium.com/working-with-queues-in-rust-5a5afe82da46","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdd0a"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/fq2NMV-QV9ayJl82ZWzov.md"}